WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.432 --> 00:00:03.255
Unit seventeen. Peer Pressure!

2
00:00:04.205 --> 00:00:10.261
Hello, everyone! I'm Teacher Vibol. Welcome to Secondary English, Level four!

3
00:00:10.311 --> 00:00:13.995
Hi, Teacher Vibol! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:14.045 --> 00:00:17.501
Today we learn: Peer Pressure. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:22.383
Peer pressure. Say it with me. Peer pressure!

6
00:00:25.903 --> 00:00:29.886
Influence. Say it with me. Influence!

7
00:00:33.389 --> 00:00:37.073
Resist. Say it with me. Resist!

8
00:00:40.581 --> 00:00:44.464
Confidence. Say it with me. Confidence!

9
00:00:47.952 --> 00:00:51.552
Decision. Say it with me. Decision!

10
00:00:55.053 --> 00:00:59.020
Independent. Say it with me. Independent!

11
00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:06.267
Values. Say it with me. Values!

12
00:01:09.749 --> 00:01:13.666
Assertive. Say it with me. Assertive!

13
00:01:17.192 --> 00:01:26.466
Grammar time! Gerunds as objects. Listen. Resisting peer pressure takes confidence.

14
00:01:26.516 --> 00:01:32.127
Your turn. Say it with me. Resisting peer pressure takes confidence.

15
00:01:36.858 --> 00:01:48.923
Peer pressure can strongly influence the decisions teenagers make. Learning to resist negative pressure takes confidence and independent thinking. Staying assertive about your own values is important.

16
00:01:48.973 --> 00:01:50.313
I like this story!

17
00:01:51.565 --> 00:01:56.754
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:56.804 --> 00:01:57.954
Resist!

19
00:01:58.932 --> 00:02:04.156
Look! What's the word?

20
00:02:04.206 --> 00:02:05.356
Values!

21
00:02:06.531 --> 00:02:15.691
Think and answer. How can someone resist negative peer pressure?

22
00:02:15.741 --> 00:02:17.048
Great answer!

23
00:02:18.188 --> 00:02:21.293
This unit's value is Independence.

24
00:02:21.343 --> 00:02:24.176
I can show independence every day!

25
00:02:24.895 --> 00:02:29.088
Great work today! See you next time. Bye-bye!

26
